1. The four ceilings are CPU time (user + system), quiet median plus margin. Medians of five
   samples of twelve fresh processes, in six windows at load 68.7-94.1, with H177's load-21.4
   window (the same CPU reading) as the quiet column:
     version 4.2-5.8 / quiet 4.89 / ceiling 12;  imports_nothing 7.5-10.8 / 7.01 / ceiling 18
     inspect_ops 39.2-45.0 / 37.97 / 95;         imports_all 40.0-42.5 / 36.19 / 90
   The wall ceilings were 40/45/100/90 and at load 106-130 `--version`, which compiles nothing,
   read 13.0 ms. The load average is printed beside the numbers as provenance, and no "red under
   load is not a regression" reading remains: a crossed CPU ceiling is a regression.
2. declaration.cost: the per-declaration ceiling (60 us, the number unchanged) now read in CPU
   (27.5-29.1 us per declaration at load 68-94), the absolute total the ruling chose (12 ms:
   H177 5.3's candidate, the quiet total plus the 4.6 ms regression it was meant to name), and
   the structural assertion that each (phase, module) appears exactly once per round (5.3's
   candidate 3). The 30% share is deleted, not commented out.
3. The phase report had no CPU field, and the wall clock of those same phases read 75-104 us per
   declaration at load 106-112 (81.6 us at load 92.9) against 27.5-29.1 us of CPU, with a
   same-window wall/cpu of 1.57 at load 94. Commit 46e837240 is that instrument: `cpu_ns` beside
   `wall_ns` (CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID / GetProcessTimes, -1 where neither exists), and a
   platform without a process CPU clock makes the line report an error, not read the wall clock.
4. Every guard of the tool shown red by injection on the final commit, with CAMEL_EXE pointing
   at a /tmp stand-in whose `inspect --ops` path emits a canned phase report: a 20 ms CPU burn
   per process reds version (21.2 > 12) and imports_nothing (25.0 > 18) while both full-import
   ceilings stay green; a repeated (declare, module) pair reds the structural assertion and
   names it; a dropped module row, a report with no pinned phase, and no report at all are each
   named; a report six times the honest one reds both declaration ceilings (86.5 us, 30.0 ms).
   The honest canned report passes (14.4 us, 5.0 ms), so the guards reject the defect and not
   the report.

